1
00:00:00,208 --> 00:00:02,038
(Sheldon:)DEFCON 1 is a crisis.

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:04,210
How can five not be worse than one?

3
00:00:04,379 --> 00:00:06,209
Well, Star Trek V, worse than 1.

4
00:00:08,424 --> 00:00:11,214
(Sheldon:)First of all, that's a comparison of quality,
not intensity.

5
00:00:11,386 --> 00:00:16,096
Secondly, Star Trek I is orders of
magnitude worse than Star Trek V.

6
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:17,306
(Raj:)Are you joking?

7
00:00:17,475 --> 00:00:20,515
(Raj:)Star Trek V is the standard
against which all badness is measured.

8
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:21,727
(Sheldon:)No, no, no.

9
00:00:22,438 --> 00:00:25,228
(Sheldon:)Star Trek V has specific failures
in writing and direction...

10
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,480
(Sheldon:)...while Star Trek I fails across the board.

11
00:00:27,652 --> 00:00:30,192
(Sheldon:)Art direction, costuming,
music, sound editing.

12
00:00:30,363 --> 00:00:33,783
You know what? Can we just
forget I said "DEFCON" and go?

13
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:37,496
(Raj:)Star Trek V.

14
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:42,337
SHELDON: Will you at least stipulate
that Star Trek IV: The Voyage Home...

15
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,250
...is inarguably the best?

16
00:00:44,419 --> 00:00:47,549
I have three words for you:
Wrath of Khan.

17
00:00:48,673 --> 00:00:50,753
(Howard:)- Thank God you're here.
- What's the emergency?

18
00:00:50,925 --> 00:00:53,965
(Howard:)I got the Mars rover stuck in a ditch.

19
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,220
- Where?
- On a dusty highway...

20
00:00:56,389 --> 00:00:59,269
(Howard:)...just outside Bakersfield.
Where do you think? On Mars.

